Sufficient clarification temperature and time should be ensured to facilitate the elimination of bubbles in the compound.
In order to prevent crystallization stones, the forming temperature can be raised to make the forming temperature higher than the liquidus temperature (the upper limit of crystallization temperature), and attention should be paid to prevent the glass liquid that is easy to crystallization at the dead corner from participating in the forming flow.
