Digital printing technology was introduced to the glass printing industry 20 years ago.It was originally printed in a single color: black, which was used in the automotive industry.
The first use of digitally printed glass in the construction market was in 2007, when the Essefield Municipal Bank had a satellite image of the town printed on the facade.
In the world, the first successful invention of ceramic ink and glass digital printer high-tech manufacturer is Israel Dip-Tech Company.
The ink contains highly stable inorganic pigments and special sub-micron glass powder particles.Dip-Tech is based on extensive research on the interaction between ink and glass. By controlling drying and microscopic analysis of printed glass products, the performance of ceramic ink is optimized from the molecular level to the maximum.
Therefore, the construction industry on the use of glazed glass, usually just print simple dots, lines, such as repeated, simple regular geometric patterns or colors.
Due to the limitation of screen glaze ink layer and screen mesh number, designers cannot achieve flexible gradual change and the effect of virtual and real fusion.The limitations of screen printing have been widely recognized, the future is worrying ~
Combined with the application of light, the effect of the whole building is more hazy and mysterious.
