Pure liquid tin and glass almost no infiltration, will not stick to the glass, when the oxygen in the liquid tin, sulfur, magnesium, aluminum and other impurity elements, the surface tension of the liquid tin changes, there will be sticky tin phenomenon.
The main reason is that the trace tin oxide and tin sulfide in the tin tank penetrate into the glass, and in the toughening or hot bending, the divalent tin and tetravalent tin transform each other, because the radius of the tetravalent tin ion is larger than that of the divalent tin ion, during the conversion process, tiny cracks are generated on the tin surface of the glass, forming an interference rainbow under the light.
The second is to ensure that the tin liquid level of the triangle area at the outlet of the tin tank is clean, which requires the normal operation of the linear motor here. At the same time, the liquid level of the triangle area and the ash accumulation along the mouth should be cleaned regularly, especially in the operation of the plate modification, tin adding and tin tank accidents must be cleaned in time.
