The cause of the fog point is related to the dissolution, adsorption and penetration of the gas in the tin liquid in the tank, and the solubility of H2 and O2 is high at high temperature and low at low temperature. The oxygen content in the tin tank is high, and the tin is above 232 ℃ .
In addition, the hydrogen in the protective gas will also dissolve in the tin solution. When the temperature drops from 1000 ℃ to 800 ℃ , all the hydrogen dissolved in the tin solution will escape, causing fog point.
Second, the proportion of hydrogen in the protective gas in each area of the tank should be reasonably adjusted, especially the proportion of H2 in the high temperature area should not exceed 3%;
After being put into production for a long time, the opening bubbles at the bottom of the plate continuously appear in the production line, which is relatively fixed in the transverse position of the glass plate. By adjusting the width of the plate and the position of the original plate in the tin tank, the position of the bubbles will change relatively.
The third is to maintain the stability of tin working conditions, especially to maintain the stability of the bottom temperature of the tank, the fluctuation of the bottom temperature in each area of the tank is less than 5 ℃ , while the highest temperature at the bottom of the tank is less than 120 ℃ , in strict accordance with the requirements of the process system to check the operation of the bottom fan, pay attention to the temperature changes at the bottom of the tank.
Lip brick bubble treatment measures to reduce the amount of pull, reduce the temperature of the flow channel, can reduce the harm of the bubble but can not be completely eradicated, to a comprehensive solution must replace the lip brick, which requires a preparation process, may further affect the quality of a few days.
