It consists of part of the HOF directors and councilors. Each year, the HIC assumes the following tasks: (1) designating or changing designated graduate schools in Japan (which accept the Y-E-S Award Plus recipients); (2) deciding the theme of essay based on choices recommended by the ASC in each beneficiary country; and (3) selecting the Y-E-S Award recipients from the shortlists reported by the ASC in each beneficiary country.
TheASCCambodiawillconsist of four to five members, including an external Cambodian knowledgeable person, a representative from each affiliated university, and a representative from the CJCC. TheASCCambodiawill be responsible to screen and shortlist applications and report its shortlist to theHIC
- They need to have excellent school records and have decided or intend to attend a graduate school in or outside of Cambodia
Application Process: Since there is a strong collaboration from affiliated universities, top 10 students will be selected and sent to YAO Cambodia with the application form and other supported documents. The deadline of receiving the applicant will be during August .
The Y-E-S Award Cambodia program is designed to be a unique, two-stage grant system.
However, there will be no specific allocation set for each affiliated school. Also, there will be no ceiling on the number of applications to be accepted at each school.
If a given Y-E-S recipient has already been admitted to one of the designated graduate school in Japan, he/she will also be eligible for the Y-E-S Award Plus.
Use of this monetary prize is not restricted, but the fund must be returned if the recipient fails to attend his/her admitted Japanese graduate school.
The Institute of Technology of Cambodia (ITC)
The Y-E-S Award ceremony will be held during February each year at the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center, a university hall, or other venue, with guests including university officials, intellectuals, students interested, newspapers and television.
Through the Y-E-S Award program, the Honda Foundation (“HOF”) seeks to:
Promote deeper mutual exchanges of future leaders in industry and science and technology between Japan and the SE countries.
For Royal University of Phnom Penh (RUPP), please submit to “International Relation Office (Room 103)”
For Royal University of Agriculture (RUA), please submit to “Planning and International Cooperation Office”
For detail information, please contact:
However, the HOF will not provide further support after his/her enrollment. During their stay in Japan, the Y-E-S Award Plus recipients may be invited to join the HOF’s social events (cultural exchanges) and the Honda Prize awarding ceremonies.
Below links will lead you to the Japanese scholarship information and universities websites.
Final Selection: During December every year, the HGC holds a selection meeting to decide the Y-E-S Award recipients. The actual number of the recipients for a particular year may vary and could be fewer in total than the maximum number allotted for Cambodia.
The Foundation was established as a result of the first DISCOVERIES International Symposium that had been held the previous year.
The Foundation has since inception held many forums with researchers across the borders and disciplines for their active discussion concerning the roles and potentials of ecotechnology. Recently Asia has been our focus, starting with the 2002 China-Japan-Korea international symposium on the regional cooperation in East Asia.
In 2006 the scholarship program Honda Young Engineer and Scientist’s Award, Y-E-S Award was established to foster the next generation of leaders in the field of science and technology. In order to attract more talented people in this field the Foundation plans to broaden its scope in the future, especially for students in Asia.
Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center (CJCC)
Institute of Technology of Cambodia (ITC)
