Why are most beer glass bottles is green?
By the 1930s, it was accidentally discovered that beer in a brown bottle tasted no worse over time.”This is because beer in brown bottles is more protected from the effects of light.”Beer in the sun gives off a bad smell.The study found that the culprit was isoalpha-acid, which is found in hops.Oxone, a bitter ingredient in hops, helps produce riboflavin when exposed to light, while isoalpha-acid in beer reacts with riboflavin to break it down into a compound that tastes like weasel fart.
After World War II, however, there was a period in Europe when demand for brown bottles outpaced supply, forcing some of the more famous beer brands to return to green bottles.Because of the quality of these brands, green bottle beer became synonymous with quality beer.A number of brewers followed suit, using green bottles.
