Today we want to bring you a compilation of the best transfigurations of two-handed swords and axes so that you can dress your character with style. Inside music and… action!
1 Best Transmogrification of Two-Handed Swords and Axes
Although in this 7.3.5 patch we have had a lot of problems due to the amount of crashes that have occurred, we have to look to the future. With this new leveling system we will have the opportunity to transfigure our low-level characters with parts of armor or weapons that surpass us.
For that reason and because we want you to fight in style in any corner of Azeroth, here is a compilation of the best transmogrifications of two-handed swords and axes that you can get for the transmogrification of your character. Some of them have a lot of history behind them, others are just there.
Starting the compilation with one of my favorite weapons, the Grand Marshal's Greatswordit can be easily obtained for as little as 5 marks of honor. The NPC selling this greatsword isLieutenant Jackspringand can be found in theStormwind City.
Also, if we have the bad luck that it has not touched us, we can still keep trying since there is another version with the same model calledSharp Blade of Slashing Obsidian. This can be obtained as loot from Onyxiaat 7%.
Despite being one of my favorite two-handed sword designs,Cataclysmic Gladiator's Greatswordis, like theGreat Marisca Greatsword, very easy to get. Can be purchased from as few as 5 Honor Marks from different Cataclysmic Gladiator Quarters found in Tanaris, Orgrimmar o Stormwind.
Hell Harrowing As with the previous two-handed ax, the Hell HarrowingIt is also obtained by loot at 11% of the bossFel Lord Zakuun, In the Hellfire Citadel.
However, if you don't want to have to farm reputation to later craft this ax, you can find it up for auction for a whopping 35.000 gold. So now you know ... if you like it and want it, don't even think about giving your money to the people who sell it.
We hope you liked this article and I would like to read your answers to these questions:
What is your favorite among them all?
As I understand it, the great marshal's greatsword cannot be transfigured, only those who obtained it at the time by means of the sand index, that's what they told me, or is it possible? Reply to brian
I've checked the greatsword theme in-game to be 100% sure this is still current and yes. The two-handed greatsword called "Grand Marshal's Greatsword" can be obtained from "Lieutenant Jackspring" in Stormwind City.
Good Adrian, the greatsword can be obtained as you have said but it cannot be transfigured since I have bought it and it does not come out in my appearances. Reply to Juanma
Apparently I have informed myself and these cannot be transmogrified, as well as some old PvP sets. I didn't realize that Grand Marshal's sword belonged to this group of weapons that cannot be transfigured.
Conclave of the Chosen Mythical - Battle of Dazar'alor
How is life going?
2 Conclave of the Chosen Mythical
His guards have thwarted numerous attempts to end King Rastakhan's life and the structure has survived hardships both in recent times and in the past. However, as war draws near to the shores of Zuldazar, the Alliance embarks on a reckless ploy to lay siege to the golden pyramid and sever the Zandalari's bond with the Horde.
We must bear in mind that the Conclave of the Chosen is "only" available to the Alliance. The horde will have to speak with a specific NPC that will appear in the band to enter a kind of "Flashback" where we will fight it as part of the Alliance.
On this occasion, we will once again have the collaboration of Yuki y zashi. Here is the complete guide to Conclave of the Mythical Chosen:
During the encounter, loa appear to unleash their wrath, and an additional loa is added to the rotation each time a new aspect joins the battle. The encounter ends with the defeat of all aspects of the loa.
Approach Pa'ku during Wrath of Pa'ku to avoid taking lethal damage.
This combat will take place in a single phase where we will have to face different loa and their respective aspects. Once we finish with one of the aspects, another one of them will appear.
It is very important to keep aspects at least 7 meters apart to prevent it from being activatedPact of the loa. Upon the death of any aspect, his loa will channel the Cry of the fallen, dealing massive amounts of damage over time to all players in the raid.
Wind offeringHe will use it from time to time on himself, increasing his haste by 45% and his movement speed by 75% for 15 seconds. This effect can and should be dispelled.
After his appearance (or at the beginning of the fight depending on who we have chosen) and after approximately 65 seconds, Gonk will give his appearance to channelGonk's Wrath. This ability will allow you to summon a pair of raptors that will pin random players withDam mark and dealing massive amounts of damage upon reaching them.
Raptor formwill transform the skin into a Raptor, allowing you to useSavage somantaover the target tank. This dot does a lot of damage and, in addition, the tank must keep the aspect with its back to the rest of the group.
Mental blurIt will be cast on multiple players, preventing them from casting spells or abilities. This effect should be dispelled by the healers.
Krag'wa will appear and channel the faculty Wrath of Krag'wa, jumping on the three players who are farthest away, inflicting a lot of damage and pushing the players who are inside the area.
Bwonsamdi will appear from time to time and will launch Bwonsamdi's Wrath, cursing random players and makes them immune to all healing effects. If an enemy dies while having this aura, or if it dissipates, the curse jumps to the nearest target that is not under this effect.
