5 Tips for the meeting
-Noura, Mother of the Flames
-Diima, Mother of Gloom
As we have explained previously, the encounter will take place with two sisters in combat and, the remaining one, channeling a devastating ability. In order not to get too complicated, we will start from the beginning of the match.
Diima, Mother of GloomyNoura, Mother of the Flames
Torment of Aman'thul: Every second that it remains active, it will increase the healing it receives from the abilityMachinations of Aman'thul, also progressively increasing the damage of the debuff to all players until we delete ourselves.
Torment of Khaz'goroth: This NPC will burn all players in front of it as it will castFlames of Khaz'goroth. We must bear in mind that several echoes will appear around the entire band and the area line will be quite extensive.
Noura, Mother of the Flames
It will simply appear a whirlwind of fire on the ground that will move slowly. The wisest thing to do is avoid damage from this ability at all costs as it deals a large amount of damage.
Diima, Mother of Gloom
The second faculty that this sister will obtain will beIcy bloodit should be the job of the healers to keep the players affected. This ability will absorb all healing received during the debuff's 10 seconds, and when the debuff ends, the player will freeze and the duration of the debuff will depend on the amount of healing absorption remaining.
Stay away from your peers when you are affected by Golganneth's Fury.
Enter the golden zones duringStorm of darkness.
Do not allow the sisters to stay within 18 meters due toShivaist pact.
Heal players affected byIcy blood.
Defeat the Torments before they finish channeling Machinations of Aman'thul.
