With the launch of Tides of Vengeance, players will have the chance to participate in faction raids in Zandalar and Kul Tiras. Members of the Horde and Alliance of level 110 or higher will be able to intervene in these events on one of the two continents as long as they have unlocked the World Quests in their accounts and started the war campaign.
Players will have the chance to participate in a multitude of types of missions, such as eliminating elite targets, laying waste to enemy armies with powerful magic and siege weapons, sinking the enemy ship, participating in covert assassinations, or embarking on shared missions that are very close to each other. the two rival factions.
Higher-level players will be able to obtain more reputation, war resources, and new pieces of equipment (item level 325-370) that can be forged by the Titans. In addition, you can get many achievements both in PvE and in war mode.
