Official Battle for Azeroth 8.0 pre-expansion patch notes that will be released on July 17 in America and July 18 in Europe.
Although Azeroth's wounds have yet to heal, the battered trust between the Alliance and the Horde has proven the most difficult to heal. With this millennial conflict reignited, it's time to unite with your allies and lead the cause of your faction.
Experience the upsurge of war without quarter in Teldrassil and, later, in Lordaeron starting the week of July 24. The contest will last three weeks and will culminate in the launch of Battle for Azeroth August 14.
The war against the Burning Legion has left the Orcs with their heads held high, a new stance option available to all Orc players. Blood Elves now have access to golden eyes as well as a few new faces.
PvP talents for all class specs have been redesigned. By pressing "N" (the default keyboard shortcut) you can take a look at the PvP talents and with "H" you can see the new PvP system.
Now you can activate War mode and go out into a world full of other players who have also made that dangerous decision. With War mode you will have the following bonuses:
War mode can be activated or deactivated, starting at level 20, by visiting Orgrimmar or Stormwind and selecting your preferences in the talent panel (with the default "N" key). Careful!
On July 17th, the final PvP season will end with a Legion and the postseason will begin. Look for the new progression and PvP rewards that you can unlock and earn after the release of Battle for Azeroth in a few weeks.
Voice chat is now available in all groups, guilds, and communities. Select the in-game headset icon to talk to other players.
Classic loot rules will now be activated by default when entering an instance that is 10 levels or more above the content level. With these rules, you will be able to obtain any object that could have been looted in a group or complete raid of the room level.
To make the numbers on the screen more visible, the values used for player and enemy stats throughout the game have been lowered. This includes values such as equipment level, damage, armor, health, and defense.
All classes and specs have been updated to Battle for Azeroth.
Adjusted many talents and PvP talents.
Consumption: Hit all enemies in front of you with a hungry attack that heals for 100% of the damage dealt
Army of the Dead and Raise Dead now have shorter cooldowns.
Control of the Dead: Desecrate / Death and Decay reduces the movement speed of enemies in your area.
Demon Hunters have a new ability: Magic Consumption, which consumes an enemy's beneficial magic effect, removes it, and grants you fury or pain.
Demon Hunters now have Mark of Chaos: Your Chaos (Devastation) or Fire (Revenge) damage marks the target, increasing magic damage the enemy takes from you and other players by 5%.
Aura of Immolation: You are engulfed in flames, dealing Fire damage to your enemies and generating fury.
Burned Flesh: Fiery Mark increases Fire damage dealt to the target.
Travel Forms now have a different ability in your spellbook.
Solar Wrath now has a chance to grant Lunar Empowerment, and Lunar Strike has a chance to grant Solar Empowerment.
Killing Instinct: Killing deals more damage against enemies below 35% health.
Optimization: Rapid Fire now lasts 30% longer.
The Survival specialization has been thoroughly overhauled and now results in a flexible character who acts at a distance, using explosives and animal poisons in addition to coordinated attacks with his pet.
Raptor Strike: A vicious slash that deals a high amount of physical damage. Spend focus.
Wildfire Infusion: Add additional reagents to your Wild Bomb, granting it an upgrade of three random options each time you cast it.
Searing Touch: Torch deals increased bonus damage and a guaranteed critical strike when the target is below 30% health.
All specs are now based on Leg Sweep: Knocks down all nearby enemies and stuns them.
Fist of the White Tiger: A very powerful physical strike that generates 3 Chi.
Vengeful Crusader: A skill with a significant cooldown that causes your attacks to heal wounded allies, increases the damage of Crusader Strike, Judgment, and auto attacks, and speeds up the cooldown of Crusader Strike and Judgment.
Unyielding Spirit: Reduces the cooldown of Divine Shield, Shield of Vengeance, and Laying on of Hands.
Selfless Healing: Abilities that spend Holy Power reduce the cast time and mana cost of your next Flash of Light and increase its healing.
Cosmic Wave: When the cooldown of Holy Word: Serenity or Holy Word: Sanctify expires, you emit a burst of light that heals up to 5 injured targets
Shadow Priests can now use Leap of Faith.
Dark Void: Unleash a blast of dark energy around the target, dealing damage and applying Shadow Word: Pain to nearby enemies. Generates 30 Insanity.
Poison Bomb: Poison and Rupture have a chance for each combo point spent to break a vial of poison at the target location, creating a pool of acid death that deals nature damage over time to all enemies it hits. be in it.
Flash Flood: The cast time of your next heal is reduced by 20% when consuming Tidal Waves.
Warriors have Battlecry again: Increases the attack power of all your allies by 10% for 1 hour.
Weapon specialization has undergone some adjustments to many major abilities.
Sweeping Strikes is now basic: For 12 seconds, your single target damage abilities deal 75% damage to 1 additional nearby target.
Belligerent: Replaces Colossal Smash. Hit the ground and break the armor of all nearby enemies, increasing the damage you deal to them.
Battlecry turns to Recklessness: You become enraged, increasing your rage generation by 100% and the critical strike chance of your abilities.
Bloodlust now has a chance to enrage you instead of relying on critical hits.
Whirlwind now generates Rage for each target hit.
Siege Breaker: Break the enemy's defenses, dealing physical damage, and increasing and increasing the damage you deal to the target. Generate anger.
Protection Warriors can now use Avatar, Intimidating Shout, and Howl of Summoning.
Threat: Intimidating Scream disorients enemies for an additional 4 seconds, causing all enemies to cower instead of running away.
Celebrate the arrival of the Battle for Azeroth Pre-Patch with community contests!
As I told you in the introduction in this guide, I will tell you how and where we can get to Winter squid.
El Winter squid is quite important since it is part of the achievement The Oceanographer in which we will have to catch 31 different fish.
The areas where we can fish at Winter squid They are :
Although in all these areas there is the possibility of catching it, in some of them it will be easier for us since there are more.
I leave you all the images of the different areas so that you can see more or less where you can find this Winter squid.
This is the first reputation that we will have to raise since it is the opposite of all those of the Bonvapor Cartel (Lashingte, Eternal sight, Gadgetzan y Booty Bay) that then we will have to go up. This reputation can only be raised by killing goblins.
If you have a group of friends who also want to do this achievement, that will be great. You can kill goblins much faster and on top of that you will have fun telling the odd adventure.
After killing goblins and more goblins (I think even my voice has changed), we will become hated with Botín Bay. At that time the npc Fleet Master Firallon will give us two missions.
To obtain this reputation we will have to rise to exalted to all the cities of the Bonvapor Cartel .
We can also help each other with a repeatable mission A Bloodsail Traitor, although we can only upload it until we are neutral with Botín Bay.
To raise this reputation we will have to have a rogue @ or pay a good salary to someone to help us.
From here is when the rogue @ comes into play. There is a repeatable mission in the Ravenholdt Mansion, which is north of Dunrholde Castle in the Hillsbrad Foothills, in which they will ask us Heavy junk box x5.
One of the best places to get boxes is at Blackrock Dungeons And as they can be done as many times as we want it is an ideal place to obtain them. We will need Heavy junk box x1200 to go up to revered and Heavy junk box x 1400 to go up to exalted.
To raise this reputation we have to take into account that it is an event and that it will only be active on the first Sunday of each month and lasts for a week. Do not forget about this because otherwise you will have to wait until next month to be able to do the missions that we have within the Fair.
We can raise this reputation through the series of missions that are in the Fair. Each mission will give us 250 reputation points and combining them with the daily and the Darkmoon Adventurer's Guide, it will be an easy way to upload it.
Hello alexchf10, I think we have already been talking on twitter. You will tell me how it went and if you achieved the achievement.
Sorry for the delay. Do not worry about that as he succeeds in asking him to have been at some point Honorable or exalted with the factions.
2 Changes in Battle for Azeroth
18 Useful addons
A magician is anyone who has dedicated his entire life to worldly and arcane knowledge since it is his understanding of the world that allows him to twist it to create unnatural or arcane magic. Strengths
It is one of the classes with the lowest percentage of life in the game, therefore it has defensive abilities such as "Invisibility" or "Ice Block".
Their burst damage can be dramatically lower if we don't pick the right talents.
Mastery: IciclesCasting Frostbolt or Flurry now grants an icicle. The damage dealt by this ability has been adjusted for Battle for Azeroth.
In this section of the article I will bring you several ways to confront your enemies and different ways to develop encounters, be it massive targets or just single-target encounters. As always we advise you in all class guides,choose the ones you like the most or come close to your possibilities if a talent doesn't convince you.
Down to the bone: Whenever you try to cool a target, you gain Down to the Bone, increasing spell damage you deal by 0.5% for 8 sec.
Down to the boneThis talent is a good choice in encounters where we only have to attack one target. It will increase the damage of our spells, making it a fairly efficient maintained damage talent.
Scintillation: Teleports you 20m forward unless there is an obstacle. It is not affected by the global cooldown and can be cast at the same time as other spells.
So muchScintillationandIce topsthey are good options for this branch. Twinkle will allow us to teleport up to twice in a row while Icebergs will allow us to channel abilities in motion.
reflection: Create nearby 3 copies of you that cast spells and attack your enemies. Lasts 40 sec.
flowit is the best talent for this branch since it is a talent to increase the sustained damage. However,runaIt is also a recommended talent if what we want is to add much more damage to our burst.
Chain reaction: Your Ice Spears against frozen targets increase the damage of your Ice Spears by 3% for 10 sec. It accumulates up to 5 times.
Ebony dischargeit is the best option for this branch of talents since its damage is quite remarkable.
It is often used for leveling, world missions ... any activity outside the raid. The reason is because it cannot freeze powerful enemies such as raid or dungeon bosses, so we could not take advantage of its potential.
ring: Summons a Ring of Frost at the targeted location for 10 sec. Enemies entering the ring are incapacitated for 10 sec.
ringIt can be quite useful if we want to keep our enemies at bay as we charge an efficient attack.
Freezing rain: Frozen Orb makes Blizzard instantly cast, increasing damage done by 50% for 12 sec.
Comet rain: Summons a series of 7 Ice Comets to strike the target and around them, dealing a maximum of . Frost damage to all enemies within 6 yards of their hit points.
Frost ray: Channel an icy beam at the enemy for 5 sec, dealing (120% ability power) p. Frost damage every 1 sec and slows movement by 60%. Each time Frostbolt deals damage, its damage and snare are increased by 10%.
Thermal vacuumIt is the default talent that we should use under any circumstances since it offers a lot of potential for damage. However, some of its potential is lost in boss encounters, although it shouldn't be a problem considering that Icy Veins increases its duration.
Frost rayThis talent will allow us to do quite a bit of sustained damage and while channeling it, you can make yourself a tea or something.
The Rune of power must be kept active whenever we have it available. We must be on the rune to receive the effect.
We must keep the Ice Barrier active at all times since it is a shield that will absorb some damage.
The magician has a silence called Counter spell. It also has the Polymorph and Steal spell, which do precisely what it says in the name.
