Today we bring you the latest guide to the final boss of Antorus, the Burning Throne. Argus the Annihilator will be the one we must face to end the raid.
It begins the end of all things. Argus the Unmaker will be the last boss we will face in Antorus, the Burning Throne.
In the encounter of Argus the Annihilator, last boss of the Antorus band, the Burning Throne, there will be a total of four phases with numerous mechanics in each of them. In three of them we will face directly against Argus (Phase 1, 2 and 4) while in phase 3, we will fight against his constellars.
To avoid surprises, between phase 3 and phase 4,argusHe will kill the entire band but Eonar, the Patron of Life, will resurrect us to continue with the meeting.
-argus: When his health drops to 40%, Aman'thul will subdue him with Temporary explosion. Players will have to face off against the constellars of Argus.
It will mark three players with a debuff that, upon expiration, will leave a shadowy pool on the ground dealing constant damage as it passes through. Those affected will have to separate from the rest of the raid to place these blisters on the edge of the encounter.
The position that we will maintain for these faculties will be the following:
Red circles:Burst of Souls
In this phase we will obtain the help of Aggramar who will launch the facultyAggramar Avatarand will grant tanks 100% more health and 40% movement speed for one minute. Additionally, it will grant nearby alliesAggramar's Favorwhich will cause damage taken to be redirected to the tank.
When the health ofargusdrops to 40%, the third phase of combat will begin, at which point he will fall to his knees due to Aman'thul usingTemporary explosion. During this phase, Argus will not be able to be attacked and, instead, up to seven constellars will appear that will launch abilities that will affect the entire raid and must be defeated:
Cosmic beaconit will be an ability that must be interrupted at all costs since, if not interrupted, the damage that can be inflicted on the target player and the entire raid can be devastating.
At a certain point in the encounter, two of the constellars will get weapons and the tanks will have to tank them:
The other will acquireBlades of the Eternaland the tank must take it to the edge of the room on another of the living constellars in order to take full advantage of its abilities and damage both enemies.
During this phase Norgannon will help us, using the facultyThe Norgannon Diskswhich will cause the constellars to receive damage according to the school of the spells, forcing players to hit the constellars that have the vulnerability according to their spells to perform the maximum possible damage:
The different constellars will appear in the following locations:
When the fourth phase of the encounter begins, Argus will find himself at the center of the fight channelingThe end of all things. This ability will kill the entire raid if it is not interrupted before 15 seconds and, for this, we must resuscitate and reach the tree before Argus can finish casting it.
If you are affected by Aggramar Avatar, you will have to protect the players who have the Soul bomb so that theSoul Bomb Detonation.
Keep players affected by Soul bomb y Burst of Soulsthe lives capped.
Heal the withered tree during phase 4.
