Oribos Exchange or The Undermine Journal Which is the best auction viewer?
It is used to see auction prices when you are not near a city or even out of the game. Formerly Blizzard had its own with which you could even buy and sell but it was closed, according to the company, due to lack of use by the community.
+The most complete of the two.
-It is not recommended for someone who just wants to see prices. Oribos Exchange
+Direct for what you need, without getting too involved: looking for prices and au.
-It is not recommended for someone who needs to see prices in depth. Conclusions
Not only because of the fact that it is more complete, but also because it beats it in fluidity and speed in searches. Oribos is not going astray but needs a lot of improvements, especially speed and search engine.
We bring you the list of changes, deletions and undocumented additions of patch 7.3.5, released on January 17.
Relic primary and secondary stats have been slightly lowered.
Flight Master License, Cold Weather Flight, and Wisdom of the Four Winds have been removed.
Profession and Elite World Quests on Argus now reward Glory of Argus and the Army of Light with reputations.
The health of the raid bosses in the Wrath of the Lich King, Cataclysm, Mists of Pandaria, and Warlords of Draenor expansions have been greatly increased. Bosses like Ra-den and Sha of Pride can no longer be sunburned.
Careers Many Enchanting materials were removed to simplify the profession and have been replaced by Rich illusion dust
There was also another contender, metatroph, I was only 1 achievement when Xirev finished, and had the same number of points at the time, as the Alliance has an extra 10 points. It was a pretty tight competition.
Note: The Demonic Combatant achievement has been converted to a Strength achievement and does not award points, but has not yet been moved to the Strength Achievements tab. It will likely be kept on the Achievements tab as a way for players to track their progress.
UPDATE (FEB 19): It was just announced on BlizzConline that with the purchase of any of the three Celebration Collections in the Blizzard Store or the new Blizzard 30 Years Celebration Collection in the digital console stores, you will get the Blizzard arcade collection!
We look forward to celebrating this occasion with all of you this month at BlizzConline ™. And if you want to soak up the anniversary spirit in your favorite Blizzard games, you can choose one of the three packs in the Celebration Collectionpacked with in-game extras and freebies, now available in the Blizzard Store.
The pack Celebration Collection essential allows you to join in the fun with:
Blizzard 30 Years Celebration Collection (Nintendo Switch, PlayStation 4, Xbox One)
Reinhardt's legendary appearance will infuse you with the spirit of StarCraft the next game you play with this tank of Overwatch. You can also celebrate three decades of Blizzard fun on the planet Earth of the future with a player icon and a special graffiti commemorating the 30th anniversary.
This sophisticated mount, which you may remember from the story "Impending Storm" in the Archives of Overwatch, arrives at the Nexus in three colors: its original look, sunset and tycoon. The players of Heroes of the Storm Those who do not have Tracer yet will receive this adventurer of space and time with the purchase of a Celebration Collection because… what good is a good mount if there is no one at the helm?
PC players will be able to obtain these items with the Celebration Collection in the Blizzard Store. For console players, these game items are also available in the Blizzard 30 Years Celebration Collection for Nintendo Switch, PlayStation 4 and Xbox One.
