Fixed a bug that caused the encounter to unintentionally reset after resurrecting a player who died in the Death Realm.
Fixed a bug that caused Enveloping Protection to be removed early when a target was hit with an attack that would fully absorb the shield.
Celebrate the arrival of the Battle for Azeroth Pre-Patch with community contests!
The Battle for Azeroth Pre-Patch arrives tomorrow in the American Kingdoms and on the 18th to the European Kingdoms. Many content creators want to celebrate with all of you the arrival of this new content and the approach of the new expansion that will arrive in the middle of August.
In these ten contests that you will have available, you will choose to get 30 days of Game Time in World of Warcraft. Each content creator will raffle a month, so in total we will raffle a total of 10 months of Game Time.
Giveaway: 30 days of Game Time in World of Warcraft.
Giveaway: One of the pets available in the official Blizzard store.
To access this giveaway, you just have to click on the name of the content creator and it will take you directly to the respective contest (remember to read in the tweet what is required to participate).
Giveaway: One of the mounts available in the official Blizzard store.
A total of 21 draws to welcome the Battle for Azeroth Pre-Patch.
In Tides of Vengeance, the Horde and the Alliance have strengthened their positions in Kul Tiras and Zandalar with the aim of taking advantage of these areas as starting points to access Azerite from enemy territory.
The Horde and the Alliance have strengthened their positions in Kul Tiras and Zandalar with the aim of taking advantage of these areas as starting points to access Azerite from enemy territory. Now the two factions will use these bridgeheads to launch large-scale assaults and enter hostile lands.
Faction Raids will alternate regularly between Kul Tiras and Zandalar so that players have the opportunity to help their faction attack or defend through a series of world missions. Similar to Legion Assaults, you can see when a Faction Assault is about to occur by opening the world map (M).
If you're leveling up an alternate character (or two), Faction Raids offer plenty of opportunities to gain experience and build reputation with the Seventh Legion or Defenders of Honor. Completing a faction assault will also grant you a 1 hour experience buff that will help you level up in Battle for Azeroth and prepare to contribute all your power to your faction.
Get together with some friends to share the fun… and protect each other. Faction raids promise a lot of excitement.
