Nathria Castle raid loot increased by 33% | News, Shadowlands | WoW Guides | WoW Guides
Bosses now drop 33% more loot than before, on all difficulties.
10-player raids should now have 2 pieces of equipment and 20-player raids should now have 4 equipment pieces for each boss. These adjustments will not affect other loot dropped at Nathria Castle (such as Memories or Legendary Conduits), nor will there be any impact on drops from raid encounters outside Nathria Castle.
The champions Friada and Ra'wani will be part of the first combat of this band, being a different commander according to the faction to which we belong.
Alliance: Ra'wani and his troops are the first line of defense against the Alliance, and they have sworn to give their lives for their city. They work side by side to empower and heal each other as they repel invaders.
On this occasion, we will once again have the collaboration of Yuki y zashi. Here is the complete guide of both champions:
When tanking additional enemies, keep them away from Consecration so they are not affected by their damage reduction.
Avoid facing allied Crusaders when they cast Blinding faith.
Avoid attacking the boss when she is under the effect of Seal of Atonement.
Tanks will need to be switched to the boss first after 15 marks as Sacral blade accumulates indefinitely.
Upon reaching 100p. of energy, the boss will use Judgment: Righteousness on a nearby friendly minion, boosting it for damage and healing.
As we have said before, in this second phase we will have to focus our damage on the minions and avoid the champion at all costs. To do this, we will start by focusing on the minion powered by Judgment: Righteousness.
Crusader Strike instant damage that should be eaten by the tank (obviously, because it's the one that is tanking it).
Consecration this area will damage players and reduce the damage taken from minions so the tank holding the adds must move them out of the area.
Divine blast this ability will damage a random player, damage that must be healed.
Penitencia will heal an allied minion for 2% health every 1 second or, if there are no allied minions, it will damage a random player. This faculty must also be interrupted.
Finally, when you reach 100p. of energy, will launch Sentence: Trial, an ability that should try to eat only the tank and that allies can avoid by keeping their distance from the champion.
When the champion reaches 30% of her maximum health, she will cast Vengeful Wrath boosting and increasing its damage by 30%.
This ability only adds one extra ability to combat. The mechanics will remain the same:
And so far this guide of the Champions of the Light. We hope it has served you and, above all, we thank you once againYukiyzashifor collaboration.
