New Allied Races Arrive: Kul Tiras Humans and Zandalari Trolls | Battle for Azeroth, News | WoW Guides | WoW Guides
New Allied Races Arrive: Humans of Kul Tiras and Zandalari Trolls
Embrace of the loa: Pray to a loa and receive one of six powerful favors.
Regenerating: You focus to heal quickly over a short period of time.
Complete the following achievements on the continent of Zandalar: "The Throne of Zuldazar", "The Dark Heart of Nazmir", "Secrets in the Arena", "Pact of Blood" and "The Last Seal". Get the achievement Tides of Vengeance.
When the next content update is available, players who meet these requirements will gain access to a quest chain to recruit the Zandalari as an allied race. When these missions are completed, you will receive the achievement "Allied races: Zandalari trolls" and you can create a new Zandalari on the character creation screen.
Children of the sea: Swim faster and hold your breath longer underwater.
Requirements to unlock this allied race:
When the next content update is available, eligible players will gain access to a quest chain to recruit the humans of Kul Tiras as an allied race. When these missions are completed, they will receive the achievement "Allied Races: Kul Tiras" and they will be able to create a new human from Kul Tiras on the character creation screen.
At level 110, and after having completed the initial quest chains of Battle for Azeroth, the new war campaign will be presented to you and you will set out on the road to opening up new positions over time in the territories of the enemy faction.
Complete the war campaign in Zandalar and Kul Tiras.
Chapter 1: The First Assault - It is necessary to have level 120 and reputation Friendly with the Defenders of Honor to start the corresponding war campaign missions and get this achievement.
Chapter 2: Marshal's Tomb - It is necessary to have a minimum of 4500 reputation Friendly with the Defenders of Honor to start the corresponding war campaign missions and get this achievement.
Chapter 3: Death of a Sabiomar - It is necessary to have a minimum of 3000 reputation Honorable with the Defenders of Honor to start the corresponding war campaign missions and get this achievement.
Chapter 4: At the bottom of the sea - It is necessary to have a minimum of 7500 reputation Honorable with the Defenders of Honor to start the corresponding war campaign missions and get this achievement.
Chapter 5: The Attack on Boralus - It is necessary to have a reputation Revered with Defenders of Honor to start the corresponding war campaign missions and get this achievement.
Complete the War Campaign of Tides of Vengeance with the Horde.
Missions: "Our War Continues", "Azerite Denial", "The Fury of the Horde", "Cleanse the Estate", "War Machines and Azerite", "With Honor", "The Hunt Never Ends", "Come Out and Plant Plants face "and" Victory is ours. "
Chapter 8: Through the Main Entrance - It is necessary to complete the "Mekkatorque Battle Plans" chapter of the War Campaign and have a minimum Revered reputation of 14 with the Defenders of Honor.
Chapter 9: Come Out To Stand Up To Them - It is necessary to complete the chapter «Through the main entrance» of the war campaign.
", "The Battle of the Ruins of Zul'jan", "We have them cornered", "Zandalari Justice", "No one will escape", "Shattering reflections", "The purge of Telaamon", "Scattered Mists" and "Come out and stand up to them."
Your first mission will be the war campaign, which introduces you to the resources of war. After the "Royal Mission", you will see the mission table, which will allow you to start sending followers (obtained in the course of your adventures) to complete missions.
Missions: "Vol'dun's plan", "Combing the desert", "Dirty work", "Classic locket", "Combing non-stop", "A message for the Zandalari", "Improvised survival", "Here are alpacas", "Delayed Mortification," "Full of Arrows," and "The Big Bang."
