Chapter 6: The War Continues - It is necessary to complete the achievement «The War in the Veins» to start this quest chain.
Chapter 7: The Sleeping Agent - It is necessary to complete the "The War Continues" chapter of the war campaign and have a minimum reputation of 7000 Revered with the Seventh Legion.
Chapter 8: Misdeed Resolved - It is necessary to complete the chapter "The Sleeper Agent" of the war campaign and have a minimum of 14 reputation Revered with the Seventh Legion.
Chapter 9: The One Who Follows the Path of Light - It is necessary to complete the chapter «Resolved Misdemeanor» of the war campaign.
Do you want to know how much you have advanced?
Developer Notes: We identified Bonded Souls providing too much healing in an arena environment when multiple members of a team were using the trait.
Sea Storm initial AOE damage reduced by 20% on Normal difficulty.
The GMOD mount now has a chance to drop on completion of the final wing on Raid Finder difficulty.
Developers' notes: As we've monitored PvP matches since our PvP mana changes to healers and Restoration Druids, we've found that Lifebloom, as a source of healing, has become too-efficient. While the reduction to Focused Growth's increased healing and mana cost savings is a sizeable change, Restoration Druids have a wide variety of well-performing PvP talent options to fit in its place.
KNOWN INCIDENCE: Talking to Mistress Xiulan does not count towards "Under the Sea," which prevents players from continuing with this quest. We are investigating it.
KNOWN INCIDENCE: During the second phase of the Niskara quest, the skill "Jump on Felbat" may not always be available at the bottom of the screen. In most cases, logging out and back in should fix it.
NOT A MISTAKE: Some players have found that their achievement points have been reduced, sometimes losing even several hundred points. Please note that as of Patch 7.3.5, several Ulduar-related achievements have been moved to the Old Achievements category, thus no longer awarding achievement points.
INFO: We have noticed an increase in interest in our Mobile Alerts and Blizzard Authenticator services due to the offer that grants 4 additional pool slots to players who add these security measures to their account. Please note that additional slots may take up to 30 minutes to activate once you have added these security measures to your account.
An extra ring with two specific traits per spec will be added.
In Season 2 and the new raid, all new gear will have a new outer ring that has specific characteristics.
Azerite gear is more flexible than normal gear, as you can change traits.
If you don't have the perfect gear and traits for another spec and switch, it will be a little less effective. This is important for players raiding the World's First, but it doesn't matter as much for everyone else.
When it comes to the cost of changing Azerite traits, if you need to change specs in the long run, that shouldn't be a punishment or restrictive.
Every time you change specialization, the cost of changing traits doubles. Every 3 days, the cost will be cut in half.
There has to be some kind of restriction on getting Azerite armor, so you can't have a chance to drop every Mythic +.
The team wants to provide you with some way that you can focus on the team in a specific dungeon, but they don't have a solution yet.
You shouldn't have to go research what each trait does, the information should explain it.
It is important to remember that tanks bring different things to the fight.
Many of the elements that make a tank expert are not quantifiable in terms of damage taken or mitigated.
There are things like Spirit Link that are desirable that are not reflected in the HPS logs.
For dungeons, Ascension seems to always be the way to go and Chain Heal feels almost pointless to cast without High Tide. There are changes that need to be made.
If one class has strengths and weaknesses and the other is a combination of all, the latter must not beat the first class in the areas of its strength or this is a balance issue.
Healing per second is important, but slightly less important than damage per second, as there are many good cooldowns that are not reflected in overall healing performance, such as Spirit Link Totem.
The team is watching the current pace of Arena matches.
If this season is known for a faster pace, and the change of future seasons, it is a valid approach to take rather than trying to change the goal immediately.
The team is also looking at the Shadow Priests.
Patch 8.1 will make the Alliance go to war immediately.
Technically, both could be active at the same time, but players tend to contribute whatever is more complete.
If you get too ahead of the beat, it's not that much fun. If you've done the whole map and have to wait 15 minutes for your siege engines to progress, it's not much fun.
In Patch 8.1, the team will approximately double the amount of reputation granted by Legion World Quests for allied races.
From now on, the team will call the new raid Battle of Dazar'alor.
In practice, the last boss can be the same for both factions.
The community will realize how important First in the world is.
The World First race is not something Blizzard created, that was the entire community.
The community values the charms of non-band content. They are created to be more interesting.
The team has moved away from the gangs as it is the only / best PvE content at the end of the game. There are many people who enjoy Mythic + dungeons.
The extraction points will allow you to create an extractor to defend it, granting you a constant flow of Azerite. You'll have to stop the other faction from taking it, or get it back if they do.
In newer areas, inter-kingdom technology is necessary. A zone does not admit 1500 people trying to do World Missions.
People from other realms can also join groups and appear in your RP realm.
Realms with a high imbalance between the factions cannot fend for themselves, as it would not be a great experience.
The team is still working on the design questions, but you want the group finder to allow you to list the keystone level, search range, bring keystone, search for a keystone, etc.
The important thing about patch 8.1 is that it is friendly with your alters.
Horde and Alliance raids will provide additional ways to raise alters, as will Island Expeditions. Characters uploaded this way may lack flight paths and equipment.
Format: 5v5 best of three
