This chain of quests occurs right after what happened in Antorus. We will know that the leaders of the alliance and the Horde They meet to celebrate the end of the war and that is when they receive news about the existence of the new mysterious substance that appeared on Silithus.
The IV: 7 orders us that if necessary we kill goblins, to obtain the samples of the new minerals.
We will also see that the silithids have survived the destruction of the area and are now being studied by scientists.
A recent arrival
As soon as we log in to patch 7.3.5, we will automatically receive a quest chain. It will start with a trip to Orgrimmar.
Upon arrival he will tell us that Gallywix has discovered a strange and mysterious substance in Silithus, which seems to be very powerful.
We will know that the Horde has been the first to discover this new substance and without wasting time they have begun to extract it. Sylvanas gives orders to kill any member of the alliance that approaches the area.
A recent discovery.
Spies are not allowed
Here you have a few images of the area in general.
When: from Friday to Sunday every two weeks from January 15 to March 7
Finally, remember that we will have the option of deactivating the remodeling of races, both for performance improvement or in case you are nostalgic who does not want to see your character different.
At this time, the entire army of the legion is at his command and they use all their enormous power to exterminate all those who oppose the will of Sargeras.
Gatekeeper Hasabel maintains the nexus through which the legion has sent its armies against the world. Through a portal that gives access to an infinity of strategic locations throughout the Great Darkness of the Beyond.
But beware!. They say that he has never failed in his missions and is not willing for this to be the first time.
The entire Legion war machine has been created by him and his devious mind. In his madness, he turned his own body over to the production machinery, to create an endless supply.
As punishment for the mistakes made, the Coven Shivarra tortures him. They strip him of his flesh and also of his sanity, leaving in him only the desire for revenge and suffering towards those who led him to his failure.
They are the most faithful and wicked followers of Sargeras, to whom he entrusted the mission of perverting the minds of the Dark Titans and being able to get a Dark Pantheon that was impossible to stop.
If someone is reckless enough to enter his hall, they will immediately be reduced to ashes by Aggramar's fiery blade, Taeshalach.
A broken soul that feeds an infinite evil.
It begins the end of all things.
