Date confirmation Update July 13: It has just been officially confirmed that the Battle for Azeroth pre-patch event will launch on July 18 (17 in America).
Tensions between the Horde and the Alliance are escalating and the battle for Azeroth will begin very soon. Check out some of the more significant changes in our survival guide for the preview patch.
The event itself
As the Alliance, the event will consist of attacking and getting into Lordaeron to capture and try Sylvanas for her war crimes.
For the next seven days, you can travel back in time, when Deathwing ruled the skies of Azeroth. It is time to re-enter the dungeons ofCataclysm.
- End of the days
Both your character's power and your items will be reduced to suit the challenge at hand, but bosses will drop loot appropriate to your natural level. In addition, in Timewalking dungeons there is the possibility of items that normally only appear on Heroic difficulty and you will gain reputation with a faction that is interested in the dungeon.
- Archmage Timereja, near Violet Hold in Dalaran, has a mission for you. Or, if you forget to accept it there, you can start it from the adventure log.
