Upon reaching 80% and 40%, Aggramar will activate Corrupted Aegis, a shield that prevents all damage and unleashes the elemental forces of Taeshalach. Then, several smaller embers will emerge from the Taeshalach blade along with two flames.
If there are none, it will hit the main target again. Each melee hit increases the physical damage taken by the primary target by 5% for 12s and stacks.
Aggramar unleashes a portion of Taeshalach's power, causing random players to ignite. Each player affected 750000 points of fire damage in normal mode and 825000 in heroic mode, to all players within a 3 meter radius, every 0,5s, for 1,5s.
Aggramar summons waves of flame that will cascade out of him, dealing 2,3 million points of fire damage in normal mode and 3,2 million in Heroic, to all players in their path and 700000 extra fire damage in normal mode and 800000 heroic, every 2s, for 12s.
Upon reaching 100 energy points, Aggramar launches a deadly combination of attacks.
Deal 17,8 million points of Physical damage in normal mode and 25 million in Heroic, to all players in a cone in front of Aggramar. Additionally, the damage is increased by 500% for 30s.
Deals 17,8 million points of fire damage in normal mode and 25,1 million in heroic mode, in a frontal cone that will be distributed evenly among all players that it hits and knocks back. The force with which you push them, will also be divided between all the players hit.
Burning anger Increases all damage done by 50%.
Aggramar unleashes a blast of flames, dealing 2,6 million points of fire damage in normal mode and 3,7 million in Heroic mode to all players within the impact radius, disorienting them for 5s. Intermission: Fires of Taeshalach
Causes the speed of movements of the Embers of Taeshalach increase by 100% within 15 yards and make them immune to all crowd control effects. In addition, the damage that catalyzed creatures will deal will be increased by 50% while they are in the area.
These fragments of the essence of Taeshalach are heading towards Aggramar. Upon reaching him, they combine with Taeshalach and provoke Flaming rash.
The Embers of Taeshalach they generate energy for 180s. Upon reaching 100 energy points, the embers will activate Flaming rash.
Upon death, the ember bursts into a pool of fiery debris that lasts for 18s. If we stay in the pool, it will inflict 750000 points of fire damage every 1,5s.
Aggramar dons a shield that makes him immune to all damage. Touching the shield deals 893000 fire damage in normal mode and 1,2 million in Heroic mode, knocking back the target.
Aggramar will periodically hurl burning debris at a player's location, dealing 2,1 million points of fire damage in normal mode and 3 million in heroic, to all players in that area.
Aggramar summons waves of flame that will cascade out of him, dealing 3,2 million fire points to all players in their path and an additional 800000 fire damage every 2s for 12s.
Uncontrolled flame
Aggramar marks up to three locations that will explode after 4s, dealing 3,5 million points of fire damage in normal mode and 4,5 million in Heroic, to all players within the impact radius. Also invoke Trail of flames emanating from each marked location.
Aggramar will summon waves of flames that will cascade from him, inflicting 2,3 million points of fire damage in normal mode and 3,2 million in heroic, to all players in his path and 700000 points of fire damage extra in normal mode and 800000 in heroic, every 2s, for 12s.
Aggramar unleashes a blast of flames, dealing 2,6 million points of fire damage in normal mode and 3,7 million in Heroic mode to all players within the impact radius, disorienting them for 5s. Use of heroism
If for whatever reason there was no other player nearby, it would hit the main tank twice and increase its debuff stack by two. This is why the tanks must be attentive and change to Aggramar, every 4 or 5 marks, depending on the type of tank and the resistance it has.
From time to time, Aggramar will use Trail of flames and it will launch three trails of fire in three random directions that will do a lot of damage to any player that it passes through and that will also leave a fairly high damage debuff for 2s, every 12s. We will have to be very careful and look at the direction in which Aggramar throws them.
First use Tame enemies, to continue with Flame tear, again Tame enemies, Flame tear, and will end with Searing Tempest.
Intermediates Here I will explain the two intermediate ones since they are quite similar although they have some small difference between them.
Aggramar is going to create two elementals called Flame of Taeshalach . Intermission will end when both are removed.
It will take place from 40% of Aggramar's life until we eliminate it. During this phase, Taeshalach reach y Thaeshalach Technique, and it will change Bengal by Enhanced Centella.
Trail of flames it will launch five stelae instead of three. From Enhanced Centella three will continue to come out the same.
We will also have to be vigilant to slow them down, root them or use any crowd control on them. All of this must be done in an organized manner so as not to cause death to the entire band.
Try not to get close to the other players and that Scorching Flare hit everyone around.
Attentive to the Embers of Taeshalach causing Flaming rash and they deal some pretty considerable damage to all players.
Today we bring you, from my point of view, the two best-known pages to view auctions with a small comparison of both.
-It can mess up a bit so much information.
Blood drinker: Drain X p. target's health for 3 sec. You can move, parry, dodge, and use defensive abilities while channeling this ability.
Heartbreakerit is not as good as it may sound. Therefore, we will choose the previous one.Blood wormsit is also not very useful since we cannot control it.
Fast decomposition: Your Death & Decay deals damage 15% more often, and while in your Death & Decay you generate 1. runic power every 1 sec.
Spectral drift: Attacks that deal more than 25% of your maximum health as damage will consume an extra Bone Shield charge to further reduce the damage you take.
Spectral driftHe could be a good talent, but unfortunately, since the new raid's implementation, he has lost quite a bit to the Tomb of Sargeras tier.Ice heartIt should not be used either, as it is useless in almost any situation.
Ossuary: While you have at least 5 charges of Bone Shield, the cost of Death Strike is reduced by 5. of runic power. Additionally, your maximum Runic Power is increased by 10.
Red thirst: Spending Runic Power will reduce the remaining cooldown of Vampiric Blood by 1 second for every 6. of runic power.
Red thirstHe is the best talent in this branch since he gives us much more survival than the other two.
StoneIt could be used but it is not a good option in this patch, allowing the other two to be much more useful.
Tight grip: Reduces the cooldown of Bloodthirsty Embrace by 30 sec, and your Death and Decay also reduces the movement speed of enemies within its radius by 70%.
Rune transfusion: Consumes a rune to reduce all damage taken by 40% for 3 sec.
Unholy bulwarkIt will be the talent that we will choose for this branch of talents since it gives us much more survival.
Rune transfusioncould turn out to be a good talent if paired with the right legendary,Soul of the Lord of Death.
Bone storm: A whirlwind of bone and blood pummels nearby enemies every 1 sec, dealing (115.9% attack power) damage. Shadow damage every 1 sec and heals you for 2% of your maximum health each time it deals damage.
Enchant Cloak - Binding of Strength : Permanently enchant a cloak to increase your Strength by 200.
Flask of Endless Armies (for extra damage) or Flask of Ten Thousand Scars(for survival) Desecrated Augment Rune
Basic attacks (Crimson plague) will grant us, from time to time, a free launch of Death and decomposition .
Dancing Rune Weaponit will reflect melee attacks and boost our defenses.
Anti-Magic ShellThis ability will allow us to absorb the magic damage that will be inflicted in the next 5 seconds.
Spectral stepit is our only and main mobility faculty.
Raise ally This is the Death Knight's basic ability to resurrect an ally.
