We bring you the guide with images of the pre-patch 8.0 event for the Alliance: The attack of Lordaeron Many spoilers, be careful!
In today's new version of Alpha, the pre-patch event to welcome BFA with patch 8.0 can already be tested. For now, only the event is available for the Alliance Let's Get Started!
With the mission we went to the docks of Stormwind and began the quest (just like the Broken Shore quest).
At the gates of the Undercity we will face off against soldiers, priests, shamans, war machines, air units, etc ... of the Horde. Be very careful to go crazy with zones or get in the way, it is very easy to fall even if we have priests nearby.
In theory we will go for Sylvanas but… nanay. Sylvanas floods the entire battlefield with blast, dealing heavy damage if you're close by and reviving the fallen by attacking you.
Don't get too close to the blast as it does a lot of damage and grows every time, forcing you to retreat. Stay close to Anduin and kill the skeletons until you leave the area.
After escaping the blast we will find a hooded Jaina fighting a small group inside the castle. We help her open the ice doors and get inside.
We will have to walk and kill Hordes until we can reach Durja. You have to be very careful with the whirlwinds, the pushes and the winds.
Sylvanas floods the entire corridor with blast to prevent the Alliance from reaching her. But Mekkatorque, apart from tanks, also brought a couple of planes.
By defeating Fangusaro we will enter the castle to apprehend Sylvanas for her war crimes.
All of these new options will be available in hair salons across Azeroth, where you can also change your character's skin color. Player vs.
PvP honor and prestige systems have been updated. Your PvP progress in Legion has been converted to account-wide honor levels, which you can earn in PvP.
All chosen PvP talents can be used anywhere there may be PvP
You can earn additional gold and resource bonuses in world missions.
Once you venture into War mode, all zones will be in dispute, including those like Northtown Abbey.
Using multiple spells and talents now triggers a global cooldown again.
Haemostasis: Each enemy hit by Blood Boil increases the damage and healing you deal on the next Death Strike.
Frostwyrm's Fury: Summons a Frostwyrm that attacks all enemies in a large area with one breath, dealing massive Frost damage.
Apocalypse: Curses an enemy, dealing damage and opening a degenerative wound on the enemy. Summons an Army of the Dead ghoul for each open festering wound.
The skill formerly known as Magic Consumption is now Interrupt.
Lesser Soul Fragments now heal based on recent damage taken (previously a flat amount of healing).
New Moon: Deals damage to the target, generates Astral Power, and transforms into a Crescent and Full Moon.
Hunters now have Command Pet: Command your pet to perform its unique ability based on your active pet's specialization:
New talents include: Double Hit: Your next Aimed Shot will act a second time instantly without consuming focus, or your next Rapid Fire will fire additional shots.
Kill: Give the order to kill, causing your pet to violently attack the enemy. Has a chance to immediately reset the cooldown.
Mages now have Remove Curse: Remove all curses from a friendly target.
Reverberate: If Arcane Explosion hits at least 3 targets, there is a 50% chance for an additional Arcane Charge to be generated.
Freezing Rain: Frozen Orb instantly casts Blizzard, increasing its damage.
Monks now have Mystic Touch: Your damage weakens the target and increases their Physical damage taken by 5%.
Guard: Protects against future attacks, avoiding taking damage that would have been delayed by Deferring. Mist weaver
Awakening: Light of Dawn has a chance to grant Vengeful Wrath for several seconds.
Ash Wake - Dash into your enemies, dealing heavy damage to all enemies in front of you and slowing their movement. Additionally, enemy demons and undead are stunned.
Priest Priests have Word of Power again: Fortitude, Increases the Stamina of all party or raid members by 10% for 1 hour.
Discipline Priests now have Desperate Prayer and Holy Nova.
Renew now reduces the cooldown of Holy Word: Sanctify.
Holy Word: Salvation: Heal all nearby allies and apply Renew and 2 stacks of Prayer of Mending to each. The cooldown is reduced each time you cast Holy Word: Serenity or Holy Word: Sanctify.
Mind Burning is once again an active faculty. Deals damage to all enemies near the target and generates Insanity.
Hidden Blades: Every 2 seconds you gain a damage increase for your next Fan of Knives that stacks up to 20 times.
Generates energy. Tricked Dice: Triggering Adrenaline Rush causes your next Lucky Dice to provide at least two combinations.
Elemental Spirits: Reduces the cooldown of Feral Spirit and infuses Fire, Frost, or Lightning into your spirits.
Now all specs have Shadowfury: Stuns all nearby enemies.
Lurking Death: Agony, Corruption, Siphon Life, and Unstable Affliction deal their total damage 15% faster.
This specialization has been thoroughly revised.
Terror Strike: When your Terracechanters charge into battle, their Terror Bite attack now hits all nearby targets, dealing bonus damage.
Dark Soul - Unstable - Infuses unstable power into your soul, increasing your critical strike chance by 30% for 20 seconds.
Overwhelm is now basic: Overwhelm the enemy, dealing physical damage and increasing the damage of your next Mortal Strike or Execute.
Tactical affects Overwhelm instead of Colossal Smash: Spend Rage to gain a chance to reset Overwhelm's cooldown.
Sudden Death: Your attacks have a chance that your next Execute will cost no Rage and can be used on any target regardless of their health.
The fury specialization has undergone some adjustments to some major abilities.
Raging Blow now has 2 charges, has a chance to immediately reset cooldown, and no longer requires you to be Enraged.
Flesh Cleaver: Whirlwind has a chance to enrage you and generates additional rage for each target hit.
Reinforce: The cooldown of Last Stand is reduced and allows you to block all melee attacks.
On the other hand, the entire Warcraft franchise has record revenues: the best in almost 10 years, improving 40% over the previous year. Shadowlands has become the best-selling PC game in history, with almost 4 million units sold in its first 24 hours.
