Summary of the Q&A with Ion Hazzikostas from yesterday, March 15, on the development and plans to be carried out in Battle for Azeroth.
The Allied Races will always come in pairs, it all comes down to faction balance.
Mag'har means "incorrupt" in orc.
Once the pre-expansion patch is live, the Artifact will still be available, but the traits will be removed.
Blizzard stopped adding new abilities to classes beyond MoP. If a skill fills a certain slot, it will add it, but having too many reference skills is confusing.
There is no immediate plan at this time to add dynastic armor to Non-Allied Races, but it is a great idea. The team should figure out how to get them, as most players have non-allied races at max level.
Guilds automatically inherit all the characteristics of the community. Communities are "lighter" versions of guilds and are not meant to overshadow them.
The ilv will allow for well-defined decisions about upgrades in Battle for Azeroth. The team doesn't want to go back to Legion, where secondary stats were prioritized over ilv.
Legendaries that are available to classes as skills / talents / passives in Battle for Azeroth will stack with Legendary Legion items equipped on your character, providing double the bonus during leveling. Top level experience
New level 10 affixes will be added soon. The team is experimenting with affixes like Blighted.
In the future world defense will return to the RP-PVP realms with the new war system.
