4 Powers according to your play style
7 Never take anything for granted
You are not Xena the warrior Princess, Conan the Barbarian or Espe and Rajoy in the helicopter in Móstoles. A misstep, going headlong or rushing in makes you lose a life very easy.
Equipment is never everything. All you need to do is know the class, plan, upgrade your character with powers, and be careful.
Without them we will lose many souls and powers, meaning that each floor is going to become more complicated for us. Kill critters, break vases and get them from other souls if the other powers are too cute and you don't like them.
Do not go crazy with the violet powers, there are times that a gray compensates more than a violet (on rare occasions but sometimes it happens). And it has happened to me a lot, getting 2 violets that I do not like at all but a green that makes me a lot of dick.
Cheer with Revitalizing Spirit, Drop of Fused Spirit y ebb.
But what has been said, this is already the choice of each one, you look at what each power does and think that you use more, what game is it going to give you and how useful they will be. Devastate the souls
Every time you meet the seller buys ALL the souls he has. And if you have something left over, if it has a maximum health improvement, it is great (or failing that, a power that you need).
If we only shoot with these types of powers, you will laugh at most attacks but you will be doing "little" damage. And with the final boss you are going to have a hard time.
Recommendation? Prioritize those types of powers without forgetting about the damage improvements, balance your character in such a way that he can do considerable damage without dying in the attempt.
I have lost many lives for trusting me, and in the Tower if you trust yourself… ..chao 1 life. Be careful with everything: with traps, fires, stealth pulls, "little angels" falling from the skies, pushing skills.
Watch your steps, go with caution in areas where you strangely see few bugs and do not stop moving in the areas with traps / angels. Be careful with the bosses
They have a bufo Unnatural power that stacks the longer the fight, improving by the second, increasing your damage done to you by 10% and your movement speed by another 10%. Mini-bosses also have this benefit, but it's more noticeable on large bosses.
