Patch 7.3.5 and the new Silithus quest chain are here. We can now play it and satisfy our curiosity in the new Silithus.
In patch 7.3.5 we will have a new chain of missions that will send us to the Silithus area. After what happened in the fight against Argus, there was a huge wound caused by Sargeras.
From that wound a new mineral is sprouting, which has made the alliance and Horde have new interests in the area.
El King Anduin will give us directions for us to settle in Silithus and let's investigate the operations of the Horde that have already started with the extractions of the new material.
The Twilight's Hammer cult tries to re-establish itself in an area of Silithus .
Mathias Shaw will speak to us and tell us to meet him in Stormwind, at the Lion's Rest. Once there he will tell us that a new substance with enormous power has been discovered and that the Horde has already begun to extract it in the Wound of Silithus.
He asks us to supervise the extraction operations.
The Twilight's Hammer cult attempts to re-establish itself in an area of Silithus. We will also see that the silithids have survived the destruction of the area and are now being studied by scientists.
We will also meet Magni Bronzebeard who will give us a message for our leader in which he tells us that the new and mysterious material is the blood of Azeroth and that if we use it for our own benefit, he will die.
I hope that with all this you have gotten more desire to play patch 7.3.5. See you in Azeroth!
