It's time for the best teams in the world to show us what they can do. For starters, we are going to tell you a few things about this season's Proving Grounds.
Like last season, we will start with a period called "Proving Grounds", in which the teams will come together to show that they have what it takes. This year's Proving Grounds will be similar to last year, but with a few minor changes.
During the two weeks of the Proving Grounds, you will form a group of five friends to take on the toughest Mythic Keystone dungeons you can. The goal is to complete a total of Five Level 23 Mythic Keystone Dungeons during those two weeks.
Repeated dungeons do not count toward the total of five, to ensure that you clear a mixed group of them.
Once the group has completed the dungeons of the required difficulty, you will have to choose a captain, who will be in charge of registering the team. At the end of the Proving Grounds period, we will post in this article how and when to submit your best times.
Here you have the official tournament rules (in English). Make sure all team members meet the regional requirements:
Pacific Asia: Legal residents of Hong Kong, Macao, Korea, Taiwan, New Zealand, Australia, Singapore, Thailand, the Philippines, Malaysia, Vietnam and Indonesia belong to this region, except where there are prohibitions or restrictions in force.
