Deep within Dazar'alor is a chamber built in honor of the six greatest loa of Zandalar, protected by their most devoted followers. Intruders who dare enter this sacred chamber will face unparalleled primal fury.
A couple of aspects join the fray early in the match, while the others watch. Each time an aspect is defeated, any other active aspect is fully healed and receives a stack of Wrath of the Loa.
Wrath of Pa'ku
When you dissipate theBwonsamdi's Wrath, it will jump to the closest target that is not under this effect.
To start the match, we can choose which aspects we want to fight against and according to the order we prefer. The loa will appear to cast their ability, and after that, they will let the aspect take care of the rest.
Let's look at the aspects and the Loa one by one:
After his appearance (or at the beginning of the fight depending on who we have chosen) and after approximately 65 seconds, Pa'ku will give his appearance to channel Wrath of Pa'ku . This ability will allow him to move to a random place in the room and start emitting waves that will do a huge amount of damage to all players who are more than 10 meters from Pa'ku.
Crawling HexHe will use it from time to time, marking random players with a large green circle that will prevent them from attacking or casting abilities. These players must withdraw from the raid as, upon expiration, all players within the area will receive the same debuff.
After his appearance (or at the beginning of the fight depending on who we have chosen) and after approximately 65 seconds, Kimbul will give his appearance to channelWrath of Kimbul. With this ability, Kimbul will appear in the central area of the encounter and subsequently mark three random players.
Lacerating clawsIt is a brand that does large amounts of damage and applies damage over time. It is the basic brand of tanks that will have to be changed every 3 or 4, in addition to having to keep the look with its back to the raid.
After his appearance (or at the beginning of the fight depending on who we have chosen) and after approximately 65 seconds, Akunda will give his appearance to channelAkunda's Wrath. Akunda will appear in the middle of the room and mark multiple players with a static area that will explode after a few seconds dealing large amounts of area damage (in addition to taking damage to the caster himself).
Regarding the aspect, we must take into account two faculties: Thunderous stormit will mark Akunda's aspect with a 10 meter blue area around it, dealing massive amounts of damage after its three second channel.
Conclave of the Chosen Mythical - Dazar'alor
