Like wild fire - Follow Nathanos to the castle.
We must find High Overlord Saurfang to inform him and receive his orders.
We will have to defend ourselves against the spies of the Alliance. At the same time we will have to evacuate civilian citizens and leave the area completely safe.
We will have to head towards the center of the city together with Overlord Saurfang trying to catch the spies who have very important information and evacuate the citizens that may have remained.
We arrived at the center and evacuated the rest of the lagging citizens and we must also eliminate any possible spies that may remain in the area.
We must try to stop the Alliance attack with all the weapons that we have at our disposal.
We will have to defend the Azerite war machine on the battlefield that will be savagely attacked by the Alliance.
Although Sylvanas Windrunner and High Overlord Saurfang have differences with the use of blight, this time we will have to arm ourselves with a gas mask and blight canister and spray the blight all over the area, annihilating as many Alliance soldiers as possible. in front of.
We will receive instructions from Sylvanas to continue the fight. We will follow Nathanos and Baine Bloodhoof.
We arrive at the inner courtyard of the castle where a large number of abominations and machines are waiting for us under the command of Nathanos and Lorthemar. The Alliance forces are under siege but King Anduin Wrynn does not want to leave the battlefield even though it may cost him his own life.
The battle is on the side of the Alliance and Warchief Sylvanas Windrunner with her battle cry orders a retreat. At the same time, it explodes the blight drums that it had prepared and that infect the entire area, preventing the Alliance from pursuing us and facilitating our escape.
We assume that at this time there will be some cinematics that have not yet been implemented in the alpha version. We returned to Orgrimmar and met Nathanos Blightcaller and delivered the mission.
