At last the long-awaited band Antorus, the Burning Throne, arrives. Put on your best gear, drink your potions, eat well and go ahead.
The new Antorus raid, the Burning Throne is situated in the heart of Argus. From there the dark Titan, Sargeras, leads his Fiery Crusade with the purpose of ravaging the cosmos.
It was built deep in the core of Argus and is equipped with an arsenal capable of annihilating worlds. This war machine was designed with the purpose of thwarting the invasion of mortals.
Their names are F'harg and Sathug and they are imbued with shadows and fire. They are the faithful pets of Sargeras and enjoy gutting their master's enemies.
Long ago, in the golden age of the Eredar civilization, a council was created to oversee defense and peacekeeping on Argus. After reaching an agreement with Sargeras, this council of tactical masters used their military expertise and knowledge to orchestrate a Fiery Crusade that devastated worlds.
Gatekeeper Hasabel - Halls of Infinite Understanding
Guardian Hasabel can use the full power of the Legion's arsenal against all who stand up to her.
He is one of the terror lords who supervised the Legion troops in the Third War and failed to stop the Lich King. He joined Sylvanas Windrunner in an unsuccessful alliance and attempted to seize power.
The cries of the torture these sisters inflict echo throughout Antorus. No one can resist their whispers and it is only a matter of time before they can bend the will of the Titans.
He is a noble avenger of the Pantheon who was killed by Sargeras and reborn as a titan of destruction. We can find him in the heart of Argus and he is protecting a huge power that could destroy the entire Universe.
Knowing nothing but pain for eons of existence.
December 6 - Mythic difficulty and Raid Finder Wing 1: Light's Breach
* Warning: there may be elements that detract from the story.
*Advice: You may want to talk to Zulu the Howler outside of Cerrotajo to get a small buff to help your allies.
Cerrotajo is nothing more than a temporary stop for Vol'jin and the rebellion, but in order to keep moving towards their ultimate goal they will need supplies, and plenty of it. You will be asked to go to the Northern Wastes to steal supplies from the Kor'kron.
Using the top-secret gadgets from IV: 7, you can see in advance what forces will be deployed against you when you assault Orgrimmar, and you will also discover that the Horde is crumbling. The trolls are in outright rebellion.
By killing a few Kor'kron in the Wastes and turning their stolen supplies over to the rebels, you will ensure that Garrosh's power structure collapses around them. As soon as Vol'jin swallows the Alliance plan, a new weekly quest will be unlocked.
If you really want to harm Garrosh's troops, you will have a chance when an elite Commander is discovered in the area. Of course, if you want to survive this encounter you will need help: these are some of the toughest Kor'kron that Garrosh has under his command and they will sell their skin dearly.
Return to Pandaria
These events will not last forever. Like other world events before it, they are likely to end with the conclusion of Patch 5.3, when the story will continue beyond The Barrens and take the next step towards what could be a historical power shift.
