Ten advantages of LED lights1-5 Advantage one.
LED light is a small, very fine LED chip encapsulated in a transparent epoxy resin, so it is very small, very light, it can save a lot of materials and space in production and application. Advantage two, very low energy consumption
That is to say: it consumes no more than 0.1W, and consumes more than 90% of the incandescent light with the same light efficiency, which is more energy-saving The lights are reduced by more than 70%. Therefore, only LED can be called a real energy-saving light source!
The small epoxy resin particles are extremely difficult to break, and the entire light body has no loose parts; the chip inside is extremely difficult to break, and there is little thermal effect that may volatilize and melt. These characteristics make the LED difficult to damage.
Advantage Four, LED lights have long service life Under the right current and voltage, the service life of the LED light can reach 100,000 hours, that is, theoretically, the life of the product can reach more than 10 years, which is longer than other types of lights.
LED lights use low-voltage DC power supply (AC can be rectified to DC), and the power supply voltage is between 6~24V, which varies from product to product. In short, it uses DC power supply which is safer than high-voltage power supply, and is especially suitable for homes and public places.
Advantage six, wide application range Because of its compactness, each unit LED chip is 3~5mm square or round, so it is more suitable for preparing devices with complex modeling process. For example, the manufacture of soft, bendable tubes, light strips, and special-shaped lights, currently only ...
