First, combine with the power take-off shaft to increase the blade shaft speed to the rated speed, and then lower the rotary tiller to make the blade gradually penetrate into the soil to the required depth. It is strictly forbidden to combine the blade with the power take-off shaft or drop the rotary tiller sharply after the blade is buried in the soil, so as to avoid bending or breaking the blade and increasing the load of the tractor.
In the operation, it is necessary to run at a low speed as far as possible, which can not only ensure the operation quality, make the soil pieces fine, but also reduce the wear of machine parts. Pay attention to listen to the noise or metal knocking sound of the rotary tiller, and observe the soil breaking and ploughing depth.
When reversing, crossing the ridge and transferring the plot, the rotary tiller should be raised to the highest position, and the power should be cut off to avoid damaging the parts. If moving to a distance, fix the rotary tiller with a locking device.
