With assortment of technologies and materials, CreateProto offers our customers a good chance to quickly simulate products during all phases of the design process for visual evaluation of features, shape, functionality and overall look and feel.
Requirements (Ideas) –> Concept Design –> CAD Modeling –> DFM Analysis –> Concept Prototype –> Design Optimization
A detailed design is generated with 3D and solid-modeling CAD programs, such as SolidWorks. CAD models are created for components and assemblies to check out the potential problems before any physical parts are made.
Your detail design will be constructed using 3D printing or other rapid prototyping techniques. At this stage your design will begin to look and feel real – it’s very exciting!
We believe concept design is critical to create a great product. Making concept prototypes before moving into engineering design phase is important as they can advance the modeling process of product design and maximize innovation.
Advanced manufacturing technologies for the proof of concept prototype that widely used are Stereolithography (SLA), Selective Laser Sintering (SLS) and CNC Machining, which are frequently chosen for evaluating concept models and design.
Prototype finishing will make the difference for a successful concept prototype. Our highly experienced finishing team offer hand finishing, primer, color-match paint, texture and soft-touch finish; and utilize a number of proprietary methods to maintain the accurate assembly and finest visual appearance.
