Rapid prototyping is a group of procedures that fastly create prototype models of a wide range of products through computer-aided design (CAD) data. Thanks to the continuous development of materials and technology, the procedure is widely used in various industry sectors.
This article discusses the most important ways how rapid prototyping can boost your business productivity, starting with simple ones such as defining your project goals to estimating production costs.
Rapid prototyping allows you to test your new product in the very early phase of its developing process. Developing a specific product usually requires plenty of time and needs different possible prototypes before the final choice is made.
It Reduces Your Product Development Costs
Rapid prototyping offers you superior control over your expenditures and allows you to reduce them while still manufacturing an excellent final product.
Cost reduction is a great booster for every business, and rapid prototyping means saving precious time during the development phase. In this ultra-fast and ultra-competitive era we live in, time is money, so rapid prototyping is your friend when you’re trying to cut expenditures and launch your hit product on the global market faster.
Another great benefit that comes with rapid prototyping is the possibility of customization. For the customers and the global market to notice your next big product, customization and personalization are something that modern-day clients expect and can make your final product widely recognizable.
Since competitive advantage is essential in product design, additionally, for specific promotions or distinguished clientele, you might want to produce a unique and limited series of products. There’s no easier way to offer highly customized products than with rapid prototyping and 3D printing.
One more benefit that rapid prototyping offers is the complexity you can reach while manufacturing your new products. In some cases, the level of products’ complexity was so great that the companies have decided to shift to exclusively 3D printed and rapidly prototyped products because it surpasses the complexity and accuracy that their in-house machinery can ship.
The incredible complexity of inner parts as they are being fabricated will remain forever unmatched. 3D printing is massively used in the medical and healthcare industries for recreating body parts and implants that regular people later get during intricate surgical procedures and medical treatments.
Rapid prototyping can help your company enhance its market visibility via market impregnation and market penetration. But what do these terms mean and refer to?
So, if you want to boost your business productivity with rapid prototyping, read this article through and then carefully select the most suitable rapid prototyping strategy for your company's needs. Case Studies
Automated Quoting Save days or weeks of development time with automated quoting and design feedback within hours, oftentimes faster.
