Ø A: Anodized color means titanium part (anode) is processed under a lower electric voltage, usually no more than 100 V, with stainless steel cathode in the certain solution. The anodized film is very thin, only several microns, and is very easy to be scratched.
Physical Vapor Deposition means the titanium part is processed in the vacuum furnace, in which the color is made by the sputtering targets. PVD colors mainly include black, gold and rainbow.
Alloy 317L (UNS S31703) is a molybdenum-bearing austenitic stainless steel with greatly increased resistance to chemical attack as compared to the conventional chromium-nickel austenitic stainless steels such as Alloy 304. In addition, Alloy 317L offers higher creep, stress-to-rupture, and tensile strength at elevated temperatures than conventional stainless steels.
Alloy 317L (UNS S31703) is a lowcarbon corrosion resistant austenitic chromium-nickel-molybdenum stainless steel. The high levels of these elements assure the alloy has superior chloride pitting and general corrosion resistance to the conventional 304/304L and 316/316L grades.
Alloy 317L is non-magnetic in the annealed condition. It cannot be hardened by heat treatment, however the material will harden due to cold working.
Alloy 317L has excellent corrosion resistance to a wide range of chemicals. It resists attack in sulfuric acid, acidic chlorine and phosphoric acid.
